<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76055" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐτῐδᾰνός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of no account, worthless</i>, esp. with regard to
			strength or courage, in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always of persons, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δειλὸς καὶ
			οὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.293
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βέλος ἀνδρὸς ἀνάλκιδος, οὐτιδανοῖο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.390
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄφρων . . καὶ οὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.209
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλίγος τε καὶ οὐ. καὶ ἄκικυς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.515
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐτιδανὸς βίην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					2.144
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>reckless</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γᾶς δόσις
				οὐτιδανοῖς ἐν ῥοθίοις φορεῖται</span>, of a surging
			crowd, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				361
			</span></i> (lyr.). (Prob. suffix <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ανός</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Οὔτιδ</span>, earlier form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔτι</span> 'nothing', cf. Lat. <i>quid</i>, Skt.
				<i>cid.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
